# Findings in old commits that gitleaks may pass, one fingerprint each: commit:file:rule:line.
# A fingerprint names one line of one commit, so the same text in any other commit is still a
# finding. tools/check_gitleaks_ignore.py reads each line back from git, before every scan of
# the whole history, and fails unless it holds only example text. History is never rewritten,
# so without this the scans of every commit (security.yml, daily-scan.yml) failed each day.
#
# Only commits GitHub has belong here: a fingerprint of a commit that never left someone's
# machine fails the check where the scans run (a fresh checkout), as 42 such lines did on 11/03.

